{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And she sent her amah.</b> In [tractate] Sotah, Rabbi Yehudah and Rabbi Nechemiah disagree: one says her maidservant [shifchata], and one says her arm [amah]. And it raises a difficulty: according to the one who says shifchata — but it says that Gabriel came and struck them to the ground! And he answers that he left her one, for it is not the way of a king's daughter to stand alone. And according to the one who says amah — it should have written 'her hand' [yadah]! Rather, it teaches us that her arm stretched out sixty cubits. And likewise you find in 'two wicked ones': שבר אל תיקרי [do not read] שברת [you broke] but rather שרבבת [you stretched]. And a hint to the matter: כי מן המים משיתהו [note: some say דמן המים וי׳] — the extra letters in משיתהו, behold they are sixty. And likewise in 'two wicked ones': it could have written שן רשע שברת [note: some say שני וי״ם] — the extra letters in רשעים, which amount among all of them to sixty."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The note abbreviations [נ׳] and [י׳ דשני וי״ם] appear to be manuscript variants: the first offering an alternate reading of the prooftext phrase, the second proposing an alternate scribal tradition for what could minimally have been written. Both are rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:35.209445404Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}